※ pl4g-test: compile=error diag=4483

※ What the attribute says is what happens when an array is handed where one
※ element is wanted.  A function that takes nothing is a function nothing can be
※ handed to, so the attribute says nothing about it.

@[listable]
fn nothing() → u8:
    1u8

let std := ⎕import("std")

@[startup]
fn main(init: std.Init) → u6:
    nothing()
